     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>Please see this slideshow, page 42: <a href=\"http://jonathantemplin.com/files/irt/irt07abim/irt07abim_lecture03.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://jonathantemplin.com/files/irt/irt07abim/irt07abim_lecture03.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792474781162000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3DC899fnDhoyndaLNdalmY\">http://jonathantemplin.com/files/irt/irt07abim/irt07abim_lecture03.pdf</a><div><br></div><div>They have calculated overall &#39;item characteristic function&#39; for polytomous data as shown below: </div><div><br></div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-xdnf1L-UDyo/V63oScRmbYI/AAAAAAAANe0/q6fDeVzDmP4fhAtDZ85608-3UOGCNIZQgCLcB/s1600/Screen%2BShot%2B2016-08-12%2Bat%2B11.16.00%2BAM.png\" style=\"clear:left;margin-bottom:1em;float:left;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-xdnf1L-UDyo/V63oScRmbYI/AAAAAAAANe0/q6fDeVzDmP4fhAtDZ85608-3UOGCNIZQgCLcB/s1600/Screen%252BShot%252B2016-08-12%252Bat%252B11.16.00%252BAM.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792474781162000&amp;usg=AOvVaw24POBDaX6PYshYkmch06-M\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-xdnf1L-UDyo/V63oScRmbYI/AAAAAAAANe0/q6fDeVzDmP4fhAtDZ85608-3UOGCNIZQgCLcB/s320/Screen%2BShot%2B2016-08-12%2Bat%2B11.16.00%2BAM.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"247\"></a><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\">I am not sure which function was used to do this calculation. Is there a pre-existing function or was this coded independently? I am very new to this topic and will appreciate any help regarding this matter.  Thanks!! </p></div>"
